+<section id="checking-connections">
+<h3>Checking connections</h3>
+<p>Connections that are kept in the pool or bound to a thread may become stale
+when the database server is restarted or drops connections that have been
+idle for too long. In order to notice this before the connection is used,
+DBUtils can check it with the <span class="docutils literal">ping()</span> method of the underlying DB-API 2
+connection, and the <span class="docutils literal">ping</span> parameter controls when such a check is made.</p>
+<p>However, <span class="docutils literal">ping()</span> is not part of the DB-API 2 specification, and many
+widely used database modules do not implement it. When DBUtils notices that
+the method is unavailable, it stops checking the connections altogether.
+In this case, you can pass an SQL statement as <span class="docutils literal">ping</span> parameter that shall
+be executed for checking the connection instead:</p>
+<pre class="literal-block">import psycopg2
+from dbutils.pooled_db import PooledDB
+
+pool = PooledDB(psycopg2, 5, database='mydb', ping='select 1')</pre>
+<p>Instead of an SQL statement, you can also pass a callable that is passed the
+underlying DB-API 2 connection and shall return whether it is still alive:</p>
+<pre class="literal-block">def is_healthy(con):
+    # psycopg2 knows whether the connection has been closed already
+    return not con.closed
+
+pool = PooledDB(psycopg2, 5, database='mydb', ping=is_healthy)</pre>
+<p>Returning <span class="docutils literal">None</span> counts as alive and raising an exception counts as not
+alive, so a callable that simply carries out some database operation without
+catching errors can be used as well. When the check reports the connection as
+not alive, it is transparently replaced with a newly opened connection, just
+as if <span class="docutils literal">ping()</span> had reported it as broken.</p>
+<p>Such a check is made whenever a connection is fetched from the pool or
+requested by a thread, i.e. at the time corresponding to <span class="docutils literal">ping=1</span>. If you
+want it to be made at the other times as well, pass a tuple with the usual
+integer value and the SQL statement or the callable:</p>
+<pre class="literal-block">pool = PooledDB(psycopg2, 5, database='mydb', ping=(4, 'select 1'))</pre>
+<aside class="admonition warning">
+<p class="admonition-title">Warning</p>
+<p>Every check of this kind requires an extra round trip to the database
+server, so you should combine it with <span class="docutils literal">ping=4</span> or <span class="docutils literal">ping=7</span> only when
+you really need it. Also keep in mind that an SQL statement executed for
+checking a connection can start a transaction on the database server
+when the connection does not run in autocommit mode.</p>
+</aside>
+</section>
 </section>
